 "source": "HARMAN technology Limited, ILFORD DELTA 100 PROFESSIONAL Technical Information (Apr 2023, document DP100_110423); curves traced from the PDF's raster chart images (spectral page 1, characteristic curve page 4)",
 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by HARMAN technology. Both charts are embedded raster images (no vector curve paths; the page vector drawings are table rules only); curves were traced at the images' native resolution with a centreline follower after thin grid and frame lines were removed by a 3x3 grey opening, axes calibrated on the printed grid lines and tick marks. Characteristic curve (image on page 4, caption on page 5): the datasheet prints a single curve (ILFORD ID-11 stock, 8 1/2 min at 20 C/68 F, intermittent agitation (roll film; stated to be representative of 35mm and sheet film)); no other developer or time is charted, so all_curves holds only this curve. The development table (page 3) gives ID-11 stock 8 1/2 min at 20 C/68 F for EI 100/21, so the charted curve is the box-speed development. x is the chart's own 'Relative log exposure' axis (labels 1-4, arbitrary origin), not log H in lux-seconds; density axis labelled 1.0 and 2.0, zero taken at the bottom grid line by the equal grid spacing; tracing noise in the flat toe was removed with a running maximum so density is non-decreasing. log_h_ref: none. The chart carries no 18% grey, speed-point or normal-exposure mark, and the text gives only the film speed (ISO 100/21 to daylight; best results at EI 100/21, good quality from EI 50/18 to EI 200/24; the ISO measurement developer is not named (exposure rating text, page 1)), so no reference exposure is placed on the relative axis. The characteristic-curve grid line at density 0.5 is printed 3 px thick and survives the opening; it was blanked before tracing and the curve bridged straight across it (x 223..234 px, relative log exposure about 2.23..2.35). Spectral sensitivity (page 1): 'Wedge spectrogram to tungsten light (2850K)'; the vertical axis is labelled 'Sensitivity' with only two ticks, 0.5 and 1.0, and no statement whether it is linear or logarithmic; values are read on that tick scale as charted (linear between and beyond the ticks), so the curve ends where it meets the chart's bottom frame, which lies at 0.05 on that scale. No granularity or MTF data are published. Not recorded (no field in this schema): processing-temperature charts (page 4), reciprocity graph (page 2, Ta = Tm^1.26).",
